WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
<b>Shiranui General Hospital</b>

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.850
I'm free from the hospital!

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.920
You're supposed to continue resting.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:09.230
<b>Orthopedic Wing</b>

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.240
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.010
Aona.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.030
Kuropi.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.820
Huh? Who's this?

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.360
My classmate.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.610
Really?

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:21.800
I'm Aona Shun.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.680
Shiny blond hair.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.370
<b>Fuzzy Shrimp</b>

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.370
I'm Washed Up

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.360
Did you break your leg?

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.010
Matching fuzzy shrimp.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.330
Hey, you. Has anything strange been 
happening to your body recent—

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.790
What is this?

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:54.490
It's popcorn.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.970
Popcorn kind of looks like 
brains, don't you think?

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:01.610
And when I had that thought, popcorn 
started coming out of my head.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.280
A mystery of the universe.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.600
But it's extremely problematic. 
What am I going to do?

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:36.340
<b>Dr. Ramune
Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:41.760
<b>Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:43.010
<b>Episode 7 "Popcorn Head - Part One"</b>

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:45.880
So, when did the popcorn start 
coming out of your head?

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.230
Recently. It pops out all 
the time. It's very sad.

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.940
Why sad?

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.190
It's sad because it disappears
once it comes out.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.310
Done.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:02.330
It's an alien. Cute, right?
 Let's be friends.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.190
He's always like this.

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:05.770
Uh, sure.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.820
So, were you getting your popcorn 
checked out at the hospital?

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:13.550
No, I was visiting Mommy.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.460
Your... mother?

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:16.190
Yeah.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:22.180
What? Hey, that wasn't easy 
to make. Why would you—

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.960
I made a promise.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.100
A promise?

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.260
Yeah.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:34.860
Pappy said Mommy is sad and had to go to the 
hospital because I make all kinds of stuff.

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:39.040
So I have to stop making things.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:42.360
The hospital, huh?

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.340
Well, whatever.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:48.450
Your current situation is that 
your head is producing popcorn,

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:51.040
and you're sad because it 
keeps disappearing, right?

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:51.800
Yeah.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.070
Then...

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.830
I'll lend you just the thing.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:00.910
Doctor, what is that?

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:04.340
An Anti-Mysterious Purse 
that traps the mysterious.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:09.160
If you put your popcorn in 
here, it won't disappear.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.600
Really? That'll make me less sad.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.600
Anyway,

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:15.920
why do you think you're producing popcorn?

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.930
Why are you sad when it disappears?

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:22.450
Ask yourself these questions 
and try to find the answers.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:25.450
Then you'll start to see 
how you can cure yourself.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:28.460
Until then, hold on to that bag.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.310
Okay. I'll do that.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:38.720
Bye. See you tomorrow, Kuropi.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:39.790
Okay.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:45.910
Got yourself a funny
 friend there, huh, Kuropi?

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:47.530
He's just a classmate.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:50.130
Oh, come on. Don't be shy.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:53.040
You're welcome to bring all 
your friends by if you'd like.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.800
No, thank you. Besides, I don't have any.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:57.220
What? Not a single one?

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:01.650
I don't go to school to make friends.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.950
Anyway, this is impressive.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:08.450
He made this thing in a flash 
with just paper and scissors.

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:10.760
Is he a budding artist?

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.930
I bet he could make something 
incredible with the proper tools.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.340
He is amazing.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:15.960
Oh?

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:21.590
He wins every art contest he enters.

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.160
He even has fans at school.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:30.720
<b>Aona Shun Exhibition
  End of Line</b>

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:26.620
When he opened his own exhibition at the 
school festival, the administration panicked

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:29.040
because it drew more 
visitors than expected.

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.370
Wow.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:34.250
Shouldn't his parents be proud of him, then?

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:36.250
Why are they trying to make him stop?

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.590
Who knows? I'm sure his 
family has their reasons.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:47.290
His dad must be really strict.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.080
Shun...

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.240
Pappy...

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.930
I'm home!

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.170
Welcome back.

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:10.320
I bet you were lonely all on your own!

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.670
Shun, Shun, Shun!

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.200
You're hurting me, Pappy.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:17.690
<b>Business Administration Basics</b>

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:17.690
<b>International Distribution Management</b>

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:17.690
<b>Advanced Business Administration</b>

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.460
I see you've been keeping your promise!

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:19.940
Yeah.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:24.330
Mommy collapsed? I'm going to the hospital.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.930
Shun, you can't see her right now.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:27.910
Why not?

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.490
Calm down and listen to me.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:34.210
Mom is in the hospital 
because her heart hurts.

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:39.190
She's sad because you won't stop 
making things and playing with them.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:47.020
Apparently she's been stressed 
because she couldn't tell you that.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:54.100
It's my fault?

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:58.260
Shun, will you promise me something?

00:06:58.490 --> 00:06:59.810
Promise what?

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.740
From now on, could you stop playing

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:06.010
and focus on studying so you 
can take over my company?

00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:10.950
Okay, I promise.

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:22.640
Shun.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:26.310
What's wrong? Are you tired?

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:27.330
No.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:31.970
Study hard, Shun.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:35.650
I'm sure it'll make Mom happy.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:45.580
I'm hungry.

00:07:48.010 --> 00:07:49.500
I'll make something.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.200
What? Kuro, you can cook?

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.730
I can at least make fried rice.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:57.180
I learned how to make it by watching you.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:00.430
<i>He's a fast learner.</i>

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.750
<i>He picks up anything just by watching.</i>

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:08.510
<i>But judging by earlier, he doesn't 
have any friends at school.</i>

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:11.510
Hey, wait.

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:14.950
You're supposed to crack the 
eggs on a flat surface.

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:16.890
You always do this, though.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.650
I was wrong...

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:26.390
It's good.

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:28.140
Ten billion stars.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.390
Of course it's good.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:35.020
Oh, right. Kuro, you and that Aona 
guy are in the same class, right?

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:37.260
We sit next to each other.

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:40.120
Then could you keep an eye on him?

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:53.450
Aona, here's some sea glass.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:55.070
I had some leftover, so you can have it.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:55.900
You can use this, right?

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.220
You can have this, too.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:01.970
So many shinies. I'm so happy.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:03.770
What are you going to make next?

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:06.100
Can I upload whatever you 
make to social media?

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.880
Sure. What should I make?

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:17.830
<i>Mom is in the hospital 
because her heart hurts.</i>

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:23.770
<i>She's sad because you won't stop 
making things and playing with them.</i>

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:26.850
I'm not gonna make anything...

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.520
What? Are you in a slump?

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:32.650
Ao—what?!

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.660
You're popping. Get the bag.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:39.240
What is this?

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.750
What? Popcorn?

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:43.050
Hey, what happened?

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:43.970
Who knows?

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.970
Jeez, Kuro, you're so brusque!

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:53.650
You're never gonna make friends like that.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:57.900
I don't think being friendly to 
everyone is the right choice, either.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:00.860
Ramu-chan, you worry too much.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:03.120
He's a good guy at heart.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:06.580
People can't hide their true nature.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.370
Those around him will notice eventually.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.690
I hope you're right.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:16.140
I wish he'd learn from my charm.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:18.270
What?

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:20.140
Oh, well.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:23.090
I'll have to teach him my specialty.

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:25.520
Your specialty? You mean... <i>that</i>?

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:29.350
That's all of them.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:29.990
Huh?

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:32.790
They disappeared.

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:39.270
Where did the sparkles that 
were inside my head go?

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:49.210
So sad. I'm sorry. Another time.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.090
Another time? When is that?

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:57.140
But Mommy is sadder.

00:10:58.010 --> 00:11:01.300
I'm sorry. Sorry.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:06.900
Sorry. I'm sorry. Sorry.

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:10.680
I'm sorry. Sorry.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.650
I saw what you did, Kuro!

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:20.960
Can't you be any friendlier 
with your classmates?

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:22.540
Mind your own business.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:26.140
Anyway, you should be watching 
Aona instead of me.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:28.170
He's still producing popcorn.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:30.180
I'm sure he is.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:34.740
If you suppress one thing, something 
else will express itself in its place.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:39.410
Popcorn is made by heating hard seeds,

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:42.300
which causes the moisture inside 
them to boil and expand.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:46.620
The shells can't withstand 
the pressure, so they burst.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:50.780
The same thing is happening inside his head.

00:11:51.530 --> 00:11:55.040
An unbearable pressure—the stress—

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:58.210
is causing something inside his head 
to expand and turn into popcorn.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.270
Something, huh?

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:03.920
Anyway, like I said,

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:08.140
why don't you express 
more interest in others?

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:11.600
Try speaking your thoughts out loud.

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.560
I'm sure you'd make friends if—

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:13.920
You're so annoying!

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:17.750
Now, now. Listen to my advice.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:22.420
For example, you could dispel your 
brusque image by performing a trick.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:25.940
I'm not an entertainer. I don't 
have any tricks to perform.

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:34.640
In that case, I'll teach you my specialty.

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:43.390
Hello, it's Mr. Belly Button!

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:49.480
It's dinnertime for Mr. Belly Button. 
Stick your finger in his mouth.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.650
Nom, nom, nom.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.890
Blech, you taste like shit!

00:12:57.890 --> 00:12:59.410
I can't eat this!

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:03.930
Ow, ow, ow! Stop bullying Mr. Belly Button!

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:07.450
Unbelievable...

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.270
Aona.

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:32.460
Kuropi.

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:34.900
What are you doing?

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:37.000
I'm making a house.

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:41.180
When I'm at home, my heart hurts,

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:44.100
so I ran away.

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:49.140
Maybe things will be better if 
I build a house to live in.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.340
Maybe nobody will be sad.

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:54.090
Forgive me. I'm sorry.

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:58.500
<i>Try speaking your thoughts out loud.</i>

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:09.410
Aona, I enjoy seeing the things you make.

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:12.950
So, why don't you make something?

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:16.960
I always thought I was bothering 
you by making a mess.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.090
But you enjoyed it?

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:23.330
I'm glad. I'll make a house.

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:25.020
Okay.

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:56.850
Kuropi, don't you need to go home?

00:15:57.290 --> 00:16:00.570
I could ask you the same thing.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:02.700
Oh, right.

00:16:03.240 --> 00:16:06.590
Where do you think the edge of gravity is?

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:09.950
I don't think there's a place
 without gravity.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:11.740
The atmosphere, maybe?

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:21.470
Kuropi, is there anything you 
want to be when you grow up?

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:26.910
Sort of.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:30.450
What about you?

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:34.680
I'm supposed to take over Pappy's company.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.020
Supposed to?

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:40.830
There's nothing I particularly 
like or want to be,

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:44.160
and I can't keep playing like this forever.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:48.030
It makes Mommy sad.
That's what Pappy told me.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:53.230
But it makes my head feel 
foggy. My body feels heavy.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:58.530
It's obvious what you like to do.

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:00.660
What?

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:04.960
You mean you don't know?

00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:15.850
Hey, you!

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:20.230
You delinquents. What are you 
doing here at this hour?!

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:23.730
No! I don't want to go home!

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:22.970
Doctor!

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:26.390
No way! I'm not letting you 
play out here at night!

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:28.220
No, no! Please! Just for today!

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:28.220
Doctor!

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:32.480
Thanks for waiting.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:41.070
Listen, I've had enough of harboring minors 
and getting accused of kidnapping.

00:17:41.070 --> 00:17:43.300
I'm contacting your parents.

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:47.620
Yeah, it's me. Can I keep 
Kuro-kun with me tonight?

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:50.550
Sure! Take care now.

00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:54.010
Nice to meet you. Sorry 
to bother you at night.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:56.400
Is this the Aona residence?

00:17:58.900 --> 00:18:00.380
What's this?

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:03.400
I received a bunch of stuff 
while I was in the hospital.

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:05.880
I gathered all the stuff 
I thought you could use.

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:09.070
This is your treatment. 
Do as you please with it.

00:18:09.070 --> 00:18:10.400
Are you sure?

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:14.950
Then I'll use this and this to make a 
Morumoro alien, and a Samihada alien,

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:18.120
and their friend Unyomaro-kun, 
and a fuzzy shrimp, and...

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:21.190
Sounds like quite the grand gathering.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:27.150
So, have you figured out why 
you're producing popcorn?

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:28.740
I have no idea.

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:29.670
Hey.

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:33.010
But I won't make any popcorn today.

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:35.750
My head's full of sparkles.

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:37.770
I feel so light.

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.490
It's like I'm in space.

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:47.200
Then try to spot the differences between 
today and days when you do produce popcorn.

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:49.500
You'll start to figure something out.

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.330
Okay. I'll try!

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:52.550
Good.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:15.820
Can he breathe like that?

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:31.520
Shun, I missed you!

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.650
Shun!

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:37.470
Daddy is here!

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:40.900
Pappy?

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:42.530
Shun.

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:48.330
What is this?

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.980
You said you'd keep your promise.

00:19:52.010 --> 00:19:53.790
Mom will be sad.

00:19:56.720 --> 00:19:58.370
I'm sorry.

00:19:58.810 --> 00:20:01.800
That's part of the treatment 
I prescribed for him—

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.550
Mind your own business!

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:04.700
What?

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:06.540
Shun, we're leaving.

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:14.620
Hey, why is your wife 
actually in the hospital?

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:17.860
What is she sick with?

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:21.760
What's the reason you gave your son?

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:25.040
Stay out of my family's business!

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:27.090
We're leaving!

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:34.430
Doctor, do you know something?

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:36.240
It's been bothering me.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:39.250
<b>Orthopedic Wing</b>

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:41.510
When I first met him in the hospital, 
he was also in the orthopedic wing.

00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:43.390
Now that you mention it...

00:20:43.770 --> 00:20:48.500
That doesn't make sense if 
she's worried about her son.

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:53.550
Shun, why can't you keep your promise?

00:20:54.450 --> 00:21:00.640
Have you been secretly making things?

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:01.280
<b>Aona Shun Exhibition
  End of Line</b>

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:09.250
You're grounded.

00:21:34.130 --> 00:21:39.370
<i>Aona stopped coming to school for a while.</i>

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:30.910
<i>Kuro, recently you've started to develop 
a sense of responsibility, just like me.</i>

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:31.330
<i>What?</i>

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:33.250
<i>Don't be embarrassed.</i>

00:23:33.250 --> 00:23:34.180
<i>What?!</i>

00:23:34.360 --> 00:23:35.690
Dr. Ramune -Mysterious Disease Specialist-.

